# D-PBR-5 evidence-commit policy (builder's call per plan §2 / §14).
#
# Reproducibility of the HEADLINE (AC.PBR.6) requires the structured
# evidence retrievable: verdict.json (the computed three-valued
# verdict + per-arm failure-signature map + measured cost) and the
# per-task disposition.json records ARE committed (re-running the
# frozen scorer over them yields the same verdict). The BULKY raw
# `claude` transcripts + per-(arm,task) work dirs + loop artefacts
# stay LOCAL (not committed) — mirrors the v0.4.0 C4 precedent of
# keeping raw runs out-of-tree, without bloating the repo with raw
# model output. The structured records are sufficient to reproduce
# and audit the headline; the raw transcripts are local-only forensic
# depth.

# bulky raw run artefacts — local only
PB*/baseline.transcript
PB*/loam.transcript
PB*/baseline_work/
PB*/loam_work/
PB*/loam_artifacts/
PB*/_frozen/
SMOKE*/
run.log

# KEEP (committed, reproducibility-bearing): verdict.json,
# PB*/disposition.json, this .gitignore
!PB*/disposition.json
